5. Dead usage_detail overlay; accumulated-token chip click repaired
=======================================================================
Evidence the overlay was unreachable from any user action:
  $ grep -rn 'usage_detail = ' src/            # production writes
  app/agent_view/viewer.rs:  self.usage_detail = None;      # the only one
  $ grep -rn 'usage_detail_generation' src/
  session.rs init to 0 and the field declaration only — never incremented
  $ grep -rn 'hit_total_tokens' src/
  render.rs  : rect written every frame; hover drives chip styling
  input.rs   : hover updated every frame
  input.rs   : the ONLY click branch lived inside `if self.usage_detail.is_some()`
So the chip highlighted on hover and clicking it did nothing.

Repair (app/mouse.rs, next to the hit_context handler):
  if self.hit_total_tokens.contains(mouse.column, mouse.row) {
      … debounce with last_usage_chip_click_at / CONTEXT_CLICK_DEBOUNCE_MS …
      return InputOutcome::Action(Action::ShowUsage);
  }
ShowUsage is the action `/usage` itself produces (dispatch/router.rs:1034 ->
dispatch_show_usage), so no second usage surface was invented.

Removed as dead: views/usage_detail.rs (849 lines) + its `pub mod`,
fields usage_detail / hit_usage_close / usage_detail_generation and their
initializers, close_usage_detail, the render block, the notices.rs tip-occlusion
term, the input.rs key-swallow + no_esc_consumer_pending term, the panes.rs
wheel guard, the minimal/api.rs surface term, and the 6 tests that set
`agent.usage_detail = Some(UsageDetail::Loading)` by hand.

  $ grep -rn 'usage_detail' --include=*.rs crates/     # after
  (no output)

