6. every_persist_setting_key_has_a_persist_arm — scanner was panicking
=======================================================================
Written this round; first full-suite run failed:

  thread '…every_persist_setting_key_has_a_persist_arm' panicked at
  app/effects/tests.rs:868:36: begin <= end (474 <= 171) when slicing
  ` but apply_setting_rollback has \` …
  test result: FAILED. 9199 passed; 1 failed

Cause: the block was taken as "nearest { to nearest }", so prose that merely
names the effect (this suite's own doc comment, and the assert text in
app/dispatch/tests/settings.rs:1222) was parsed as a dispatch site.

Fix: only whitespace may separate `Effect::PersistSetting` from `{`; the block
end is found by depth counting that skips string literals; plus two
self-checks — every struct literal must be classified (literal key or
runtime-built) and the site count must exceed 50, otherwise the test reports
that the scanner itself is broken rather than reporting a clean sweep.

  $ cargo test -p xai-grok-pager --offline --lib -- every_persist_setting_key_has_a_persist_arm
  test app::effects::tests::every_persist_setting_key_has_a_persist_arm ... ok
  test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed

  Real dispatch sites in the crate: 97
  $ grep -rn 'Effect::PersistSetting {' --include=*.rs src/ | wc -l

Non-vacuity — rename the persist arm's key in app/effects/helpers.rs
(restored byte-identically):
  "session.auto_retry_incomplete_end_turn" => {   ->   "…_TYPO" => {

  1 PersistSetting key(s) have no arm in `persist_setting`, so toggling them
  in /settings can never persist:
  [("session.auto_retry_incomplete_end_turn", "setters.rs")]
  test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed
  RESTORED_BYTE_IDENTICAL

